---
title: Nanaimo bars
servings: 25
yield: 25 squares
tags: [canadian, vegetarian, christmas, winter, make-ahead]
cuisine: canadian
time: 2 hours 25 minutes
source: Nanaimo Bars by PJ Hamel, King Arthur Baking, https://www.kingarthurbaking.com/recipes/nanaimo-bars-recipe
---

Heat the oven to 350°F. Lightly grease a #9-inch square pan{}(or 11 x 7-inch).

== Crust ==

Beat the @unsalted butter{113%g}(melted), @granulated sugar{50%g},
@cocoa powder{28%g}(unsweetened, Dutch-process or natural), @eggs{1},
@sweetened shredded coconut{85%g}(or 53 g unsweetened),
@walnuts{57%g}(chopped, or pecans), @vanilla extract{1%tsp} and
@graham cracker crumbs{200%g} on medium speed until combined.

Press it into the pan and bake ~{10%minutes}. Let it cool.

== Filling ==

Beat the @unsalted butter{113%g}(room-temperature), @table salt{1/4%tsp},
half of the @confectioners' sugar{227%g}(sifted) and
@vanilla extract{1/2%tsp} until smooth.

In a small bowl, stir the @instant vanilla pudding mix{21%g} with the
@milk{2%tbsp} until thick and smooth. Mix it into the butter, then beat in the
rest of the sugar until smooth.

Spread it over the cooled crust, cover, and chill until firm.

== Icing ==

Heat the @bittersweet chocolate{170%g}(wafers, or semisweet chips) with the
@heavy cream{57%g} until the cream steams, then stir until smooth.

Spread it over the filling and chill until set. Cut into 1 3/4-inch squares.

> Keeps a week covered in the fridge, and freezes well. A 9 x 13-inch pan gives
> about 4 dozen thinner bars with the same amounts and times.
